p Last updated October 28, 2026.

p
  | This privacy policy applies to the apps and this website published by Cezary Wojcik. The same policy covers every app that links here.

h2 Information the apps collect

p
  | The apps do not collect personal information. There is no account. An app does not send your content, history, or settings to me, and it does not include third-party analytics, advertising, or tracking. What you save stays on your device and is removed when you delete the app.

h2 Permissions

p
  | An app may ask for a permission, such as location or notifications, only while you are using a feature that needs it. You can turn permissions off in your device settings. Information from a permission stays on your device, except when a feature has to ask another service for an answer, such as a map or a public dataset for a place you picked. That request goes to the service that provides the answer. I do not receive a copy of it.

p
  | Apple, and any other service an app contacts, handles those requests under its own policy.
  a(href="https://www.apple.com/legal/privacy/")  Apple's privacy policy
  |  describes how Apple handles that.

h2 This website

p
  | cezarywojcik.com is separate from the apps. The contact form emails me what you submit, including your IP address, so I can reply. Blog posts may load comments from Disqus, which uses its own policy. The apps do not include either of those.

h2 Children

p The apps and this website are not directed at children under 13, and the apps do not collect personal information from anyone.

h2 Changes

p If this policy changes, the new version will be posted on this page. The date at the top is the latest revision.

